We just released a new version of setools.  No major changes this time,
but a lot of bug fixes, some simplification of the analysis tool (apol)
user interface, a couple of new policy configuration management features
in the editing tool (sepcut), and various minor things.  You can see the
change log and download the complete tar source file at
www.tresys.com/selinux.  Attached is a patch file to bring the source
tree at sourceforge up to date.  

Frank

